# Prospective option-resumption metadata amendment r2

Actual author: `/root`, 2026-10-10 UTC. Apply this NEW amendment after preserved metadata draft `1612b14d7549b7fb406cbef8e127440dcfddaf30548ef29d217bc49aefb6c854` and amendment r1 `5f7f6a2c45dd6a0b51c7a912b28fd49badd9aa3aa2eac8632e9b9781c201b57b`. Where statements differ, r2 is operative. Both prior documents and freezes remain immutable. This correction responds to actual public review `7ea532ffae2c839dbb08376dd9c97b6200564e711cdb2e9e42a753ff24356d3e`, execution receipt `a9576860304bdfdc50d60b9cd7e43d1ce3c0a90c6e4964f64cf7a525ff42f433`. No corpus checker source, fixture or import existed under r1 at the formal engineer's reported hold; previous task-solver evidence remains unchanged. No candidate production or data approval is authorized here.

## Acyclic member custody

`pair_record_hashes` is forbidden inside every canonical `family_control_claims` entry, whether its owner is a pair member or a nonmember. Reject it as an unsupported canonical claim field. Do not exclude nested hash fields from the established full-record hashing rule, change record hashing, or introduce a dependency-order exception. All other r1 permitted claim fields remain as published.

Canonical claims contain actual ordered pair IDs and a safe external manifest path. Compute full records with the established top-level `record_hash` exclusion, then freeze complete PENDING candidate bytes, then construct the external manifest. A manifest entry may optionally contain `pair_record_hashes`, an ordered list of exactly two lowercase 64-character SHA256 strings equal to the complete resolved member record hashes in the same order. The checker independently recomputes those hashes whether this external annotation is present or absent. No candidate field contains the manifest hash. The raw manifest's actual hash is reported in a separately frozen external ledger. Manifest member hashes and candidate SHA therefore consume already computed candidate content without feeding back into it.

The six operative public source paths required in manifest `source_bindings` are:

- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_V1.md`
- `research/curricula/RSM-OPTION-RESUMPTION-PROSPECTIVE-20261010.md`
- `research/curricula/RSM-OPTION-RESUMPTION-CONFIG-20261010.json`
- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1.md`
- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1_AMENDMENT_R1.md`
- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1_AMENDMENT_R2.md`

Supply and verify their actual raw bytes and lowercase SHA256 values. This replaces r1's five-source completeness requirement with six sources. The external source-freeze receipt does not include its own hash in its own contents; archive hashes are likewise computed before the receipt is written. Missing any operative raw source remains UNKNOWN/failure.

## Identifier and descriptor typing

`control_id` is a nonempty JSON string in every claim and manifest pair entry. No private grammar, prefix, numeric encoding or source-coordinate spelling is required. Lookup still uses `(control_id, normalized name/property, ordered pair IDs)`; sharing an ID across different names remains legal. Name/property requirements, scalar semantics and member order are unchanged.

Canonical `skill_tags` retain their established string-descriptor meaning. This amendment introduces no closed per-row property vocabulary, tag-based proof or inferred truth rule. Required relationships come from actual tasks, execution, custody and pair resolution, with independent semantic review of descriptors.

## Unchanged semantics and prospective gates

All r1 task semantics, stronger retained-frame/control obligations, configured bounds, difficulty explanations, optional witnesses, three graph-normalization views and accepted-projection custody remain required. Proposed 12 source families, 108 typed tasks, 216 views, 300 named pairs, 1,944 owner claims and split assignment remain prospective and unchanged. This amendment adds no generated semantics and supplies no implementation verdict.

Before first corpus-checker import or execution freeze all six public sources, actual target-free legacy bytes, checker source, fixtures and tests. Test forbidden canonical hashes, valid external hashes, wrong/missing/reordered external hashes, nonempty control IDs and every other supplied interface form. Preserve all failures and any superseded source versions. Generic-validator integration and actual producer graph novelty remain later separately authorized gates; handwritten feasibility cannot approve a production cohort. Common-model risk, public-design/review/adjudication overlap, feasibility reuse, finite-program shortcuts and exposed development data remain disclosed.
